+## 7. Product surface freeze (Core vs the rest)
+
+For pilots the product is frozen to a **Core** surface. Source of truth:
+[`src/lib/productSurface.manifest.json`](src/lib/productSurface.manifest.json); evidence table:
+[`docs/product-surface.md`](docs/product-surface.md) (generated by `scripts/gen-product-surface.mjs` from `src/App.tsx`,
+`DashboardNav.tsx`, imports, migrations and test files — source text only, nothing executed).
+
+**Mechanism** (reuses the `feature_flags` system from `20270411000100_feature_flags.sql`; no new tables):
+
+| Piece | Where | Behaviour |
+|---|---|---|
+| Tier rules | `src/lib/productSurface.ts` | longest-prefix match on a normalised path (case-insensitive, decoded, trailing-slash tolerant); `exact` entries match only themselves |
+| Nav | `DashboardNav.tsx` → `filterNav` | Core always; Secondary only with `full_navigation`; Unverified only with `experimental_surface` (shown with a **Beta** badge) |
+| Routes | `ExperimentalSurfaceGuard` wrapping `<Routes>` in `App.tsx` | unverified paths redirect to `/dashboard` + toast unless `experimental_surface`; waits for the flag lookup, fails closed after 4 s; Core/Secondary routes are never touched |
+| Flags | migration `20271231130000_product_surface_freeze_flag.sql` | both flags seeded `enabled=true, rollout_pct=0` (overrides only); existing owner tenants grandfathered ON via `surface_grandfather_existing_tenants()` (service-role only, idempotent, audited by `feature_flag_audit`) |
+
+**Server-side enforcement.** Hiding pages alone left their backends callable, so the 12 edge functions behind
+unverified pages (`business-decision-engine`, `business-drift-scan`, `business-scientist-cycle`, `cash-flow-war-room`,
+`causal-shock-simulator`, `causal-world-simulator`, `flywheel-engine`, `identity-signal-scan`, `opportunity-cost-scan`,
+`outcome-benchmark-advisor`, `switching-shield`, `workforce-equilibrium-engine`) call `userHasFlag()`
+(`supabase/functions/_shared/surfaceGate.ts` → SQL `user_flag_is_on(user, key)`, migration `20271231140000`, service-role only,
+fail closed) and return `403 feature_not_enabled` without `experimental_surface`; cron sweeps (`switching-shield`,
+`flywheel-engine`) skip such accounts. `npm run docs:surface:check` fails if a function behind an unverified page lacks the
+gate. `mcp-server` is exempt (generic endpoint). RLS and all other authorization are unchanged.
+
+**Security fix found on the way — `flywheel-engine` was unauthenticated.** It ran with the service-role key and trusted
+`single_user_id` from the body; with the default `verify_jwt` the public anon key sufficed, so anyone could trigger a sweep of
+all accounts or write flywheel rows for any tenant. It now accepts only `X-Cron-Secret` (= `CRON_SECRET`, constant-time
+compare) or a signed-in user acting on their **own** account. **Deploy note:** whatever schedules `flywheel-engine` must now
+send the `X-Cron-Secret` header, and `CRON_SECRET` must be set, or the sweep will return 401.
+
